  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Is My Website Ready for AI Search Engines?",
    "text": "Is My Website Ready for AI Search Engines?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "It's a valid question as the digital landscape shifts towards AI-powered answer engines. Many businesses wonder if their existing website can simply adapt or if a complete overhaul is necessary. The good news is that many foundational elements of a healthy website are still relevant. However, AI systems have specific preferences that might not be met by a traditional website setup. They're looking for clear, fact-dense, and easily accessible information, often formatted in structured ways. If your site is struggling to appear in AI Overviews or getting cited, chances are there are some fundamental areas that need attention.\n\n### When Professional Guidance Helps\n\n*   **You have crawl or indexing problems:** If your site isn't being fully crawled or indexed by traditional search engines, AI systems will struggle even more. Issues like restrictive `robots.txt` files or server errors can be showstoppers.\n*   **You operate in competitive local markets:** In areas where directories and aggregators dominate AI answers, it's harder for individual businesses to stand out. A professional can help build an ",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "AI Visibility Solutions",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
